WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.900
The "sound" of something being hot and humid]

01:30.980 --> 01:32.770
Himaraya 3rd Technical School
After Class

01:38.000 --> 01:38.690
Tap

01:46.160 --> 01:48.800
AAAAAARGH!!!

01:48.800 --> 01:53.800
Even if He is, He Wouldn't Tell Some Jerk in Fake Glasses.

01:53.800 --> 01:56.300
Glasses Club

01:54.390 --> 01:57.200
One, two, three, four.

01:57.200 --> 02:00.010
Two, two, three, four.

02:00.300 --> 02:02.840
Three, two, three, four.

02:02.840 --> 02:05.930
Five, two, three, four...

02:05.940 --> 02:07.530
Six, two...

02:07.820 --> 02:08.680
Crack

02:13.020 --> 02:17.620
What if I missed an important
sound because of your wailing?

02:17.620 --> 02:18.950
What kind of important sound?

02:19.430 --> 02:21.230
Like a school announcement,

02:21.230 --> 02:23.960
or the sound of Soma-senpai crying for help.

02:24.210 --> 02:27.410
The club president, crying for help?
Like that would ever happen!

02:27.880 --> 02:30.290
The president is the strongest man alive!

02:28.810 --> 02:30.290
Invincible

02:30.520 --> 02:32.050
You don't get it.

02:32.050 --> 02:35.520
No matter how strong a man is,
he'll still be afraid of something.

02:35.520 --> 02:38.050
Then what's the president afraid of?

02:38.390 --> 02:39.960
Well, um...

02:40.540 --> 02:43.300
It's unusual for Akira to be
late to a club meeting.

02:43.630 --> 02:46.680
Shiro-chan made him run an errand.

02:46.680 --> 02:49.680
He said it was punishment for putting
a hole in Shiro-chan's overalls.

02:49.680 --> 02:52.860
Then I'll go help Soma-senpai!

02:53.110 --> 02:55.840
If you help him, it defeats the
purpose of the punishment.

02:55.840 --> 02:57.980
That's true, but...

02:57.980 --> 02:59.870
Nobody likes a stalker.

02:59.990 --> 03:02.860
Nobody likes a stalker.

03:03.160 --> 03:04.920
When Soma-kun gets back,

03:04.920 --> 03:09.620
I'll ask him if he wants to try the new
tapioca-agar-flavored cream puffs.

03:09.620 --> 03:13.240
Tapioca and agar. They're both flavorless.

03:09.620 --> 03:15.670
Tapioca

03:09.620 --> 03:15.670
Agar

03:13.240 --> 03:15.360
I can't imagine what that would taste like.

03:21.100 --> 03:22.460
Shing

03:22.680 --> 03:25.600
I thought something was there,
but it's just a bug.

03:25.600 --> 03:27.120
Damn thing really startled me.

03:27.950 --> 03:29.580
What's for dinner tonight?

03:29.580 --> 03:32.700
Last night was curry rice,
two nights ago was curry,

03:30.330 --> 03:37.240
Curry
Rice

03:32.700 --> 03:37.240
so it's most likely that tonight will
be curry ramen or curry somen.

03:34.170 --> 03:37.240
Curry
Ramen

03:34.790 --> 03:37.240
Curry
Somen

03:37.560 --> 03:41.370
Actually, now I'm really in the
mood for omelet katsu rice.

03:38.710 --> 03:41.370
Omelet
Katsu Rice

03:41.370 --> 03:43.740
No, I just ate that last week.

03:44.300 --> 03:46.670
Hmm?

03:44.940 --> 03:46.670
I feel like I might have
eaten it this week, too.

03:46.670 --> 03:48.110
More importantly,

03:48.110 --> 03:52.170
there's the question of whether it'll be
curry ramen or curry somen tonight.

03:52.170 --> 03:54.260
Curry pasta's also a possibility.

03:54.480 --> 03:57.020
Shoooom

03:57.890 --> 04:00.750
This is no time for a long internal monologue.

04:00.990 --> 04:05.010
Shirogane asking me to run that
stupid errand made me late as it is.

04:05.010 --> 04:06.520
Everyone's waiting for me.

04:06.810 --> 04:08.480
Okay. Let's go!

04:11.410 --> 04:13.130
Now, get out of the way!

04:13.130 --> 04:15.900
If you don't, I'll step on you!
You stupid bug!

04:15.900 --> 04:18.140
Shoomoomoom

04:21.420 --> 04:25.330
I suddenly have a stomachache.
Maybe I'll go home early.

04:25.660 --> 04:28.310
I'd like to go to club,
but I don't have a choice.

04:28.310 --> 04:30.080
Can't do much about a stomachache.

04:30.080 --> 04:33.420
Shoomoomoom

04:34.600 --> 04:36.190
Teacher, listen.

04:37.410 --> 04:39.010
Teacher, listen.

04:39.010 --> 04:44.280
Today on the way home, I found
some fluffy cotton candy.

04:39.820 --> 04:52.000
X Month O Day
Teacher, listen.
Today on the way home,
I found some fluffy cotton candy.
It sure was fluffy,
but I got told not to eat it.
How come?

04:44.280 --> 04:50.210
I said to Hikaru, it sure is fluffy,
but he told me not to eat it.

04:50.210 --> 04:51.720
I wonder how come?

04:52.420 --> 04:56.520
Teacher, listen. It turns out that
cotton candy was a UFO.

04:52.930 --> 04:57.690
X month [] day

04:57.080 --> 05:00.100
A bunch of tiny aliens came out of it.

05:00.490 --> 05:03.660
It took past midnight to catch them all.

05:04.280 --> 05:06.720
Hikaru-kun stayed up with me.

05:04.720 --> 05:09.890
X Month ▲ Day
Teacher, listen.
It turns out that cotton candy
was a UFO. A bunch of
tiny aliens came out of it.
It took past midnight
to catch them all.
Hikaru-kun stayed up with me.
It was fun staying
up all night together!

05:06.720 --> 05:09.360
It was fun staying up all night together!

05:10.220 --> 05:11.820
Teacher, listen.

05:10.620 --> 05:15.540
X month [] day

05:11.820 --> 05:14.560
Those aliens turned out to be real bad guys.

05:15.540 --> 05:18.050
They eat their friends.

05:18.050 --> 05:22.370
I thought they might eat me and
Hikaru-kun too. I got really scared.

05:23.140 --> 05:27.140
Mom saved us, but I felt really frustrated.

05:27.140 --> 05:31.360
At times like these, a man
needs to be cool and fight.

05:31.360 --> 05:34.970
Next time I see an alien,
I'm gonna beat it myself!

05:37.570 --> 05:39.220
Soma Akira.

05:39.220 --> 05:43.360
Have you become the kind of man you
would have been proud of back then?

05:48.360 --> 05:50.490
The match we started all those years ago...

05:50.490 --> 05:52.550
I'm going to settle it now!

05:58.930 --> 06:00.670
I'm capable of defeating this opponent!

06:00.930 --> 06:01.930
Let us...

06:03.450 --> 06:05.170
Snap

06:04.090 --> 06:05.170
...settle this!

06:07.950 --> 06:09.260
Whoosh...

06:09.660 --> 06:10.920
Ching

06:11.160 --> 06:13.930
Senpai's really late...

06:16.810 --> 06:18.180
Well, then.

06:19.350 --> 06:20.900
Shall we begin our club activities?

06:20.900 --> 06:22.450
I'll help out!

06:22.450 --> 06:24.740
Me too! I'll help out too!

06:24.930 --> 06:26.740
Then I'll help too.

06:27.490 --> 06:29.370
Machinery Class Preparation Room

06:31.440 --> 06:32.540
Soma?

06:32.970 --> 06:34.960
What are you doing?

06:34.960 --> 06:38.460
He ran out of luck the minute he set
foot in a technical high school!

06:39.620 --> 06:43.130
Reason for loan:
Defense of Earth

06:39.970 --> 06:44.130
I'm going to show him what
an angry human can do!

06:46.840 --> 06:48.220
Prepare yourself!

06:47.720 --> 06:51.100
Follow the safety precautions.

06:51.100 --> 06:52.200
Boom!

06:52.200 --> 06:53.240
Swish!

06:53.240 --> 06:54.600
Shash!

06:55.930 --> 06:58.080
Baaam!

06:58.300 --> 07:01.400
This ultimate armor doesn't leave
room for a mosquito to enter

07:01.400 --> 07:03.360
and nullifies all attacks.

07:03.730 --> 07:09.620
This ultimate weapon can reach a temperature
of 550 degrees. Anything it touches

07:03.890 --> 07:07.370
This ultimate weapon can reach
a temperature of 550 degrees.

07:07.370 --> 07:09.620
Anything it touches turns to ash.

07:08.360 --> 07:09.620
turns to ash.

07:10.050 --> 07:14.330
Shashh!

07:10.410 --> 07:12.460
Can a mere bug like you hope to win?

07:12.460 --> 07:14.330
No! You cannot possibly win!

07:17.230 --> 07:19.330
Come at me from any angle!

07:24.880 --> 07:26.000
Damn.

07:26.070 --> 07:27.010
Twang!

07:27.360 --> 07:30.960
I should have borrowed the one
with the 30 meter cord!

07:38.850 --> 07:40.650
I-It disappeared!

07:42.650 --> 07:43.440
You bastard!

07:43.440 --> 07:45.950
Stop jumping around!

07:47.520 --> 07:50.540
Ugggh

07:48.480 --> 07:50.530
I'm getting dizzy.

07:52.540 --> 07:53.820
I feel sick.

07:53.930 --> 07:55.390
Twang!

08:01.380 --> 08:02.850
Oh no!

08:02.850 --> 08:05.180
My ultimate weapon!

08:18.690 --> 08:21.820
Sluuuugh

08:22.060 --> 08:26.960
Hey now...

08:22.120 --> 08:23.800
Hey now, hey now.

08:23.800 --> 08:26.960
What about developing the X-Ray Glasses?

08:27.430 --> 08:28.800
What about them?

08:28.800 --> 08:31.200
Oh, I don't know.

08:31.490 --> 08:34.700
You're so annoying.

08:31.550 --> 08:34.750
You're so annoying. Why not
make them yourself?

08:34.940 --> 08:37.060
Fine, I get it.

08:36.470 --> 08:37.950
Finish X-Ray Glasses alone.

08:37.060 --> 08:39.890
But when I complete
the X-Ray Glasses myself

08:37.970 --> 08:41.250
Finish X-Ray Glasses alone.
Get praised by club president.

08:39.470 --> 08:41.250
Become vice president.

08:39.890 --> 08:41.720
and get promoted to vice president,

08:41.720 --> 08:43.620
don't come crying to me, okay?

08:43.180 --> 08:44.950
Boom!

08:46.120 --> 08:47.220
30 minutes later.

08:52.540 --> 08:54.690
This isn't a glasses club.

08:55.040 --> 08:59.640
It's just a bunch of high school guys
in glasses hanging out together.

09:03.920 --> 09:06.330
No, this isn't over yet!

09:06.330 --> 09:09.320
I may not have a weapon, but as long
as I have the ultimate armor,

09:08.650 --> 09:10.860
As long as I have the ultimate armor.

09:08.650 --> 09:10.860
Invincible

09:09.320 --> 09:10.860
I am invincible!

09:11.080 --> 09:12.580
Well? What will you do?

09:17.300 --> 09:19.370
In the face of the ultimate armor,

09:19.370 --> 09:21.240
you can't raise a scythe
against me, can you?

09:22.010 --> 09:22.540
Kssssshk

09:24.480 --> 09:25.640
It itches!

09:24.660 --> 09:26.730
Tingle Tingle

09:24.660 --> 09:26.730
Prickle Prickle

09:27.410 --> 09:28.410
Why?!

09:27.750 --> 09:31.000
Twinge Twinge

09:27.750 --> 09:31.000
Rustle Rustle

09:27.750 --> 09:31.000
Steam Steam

09:27.750 --> 09:31.000
Tingle Tingle

09:28.410 --> 09:31.000
Why is my back so violently itchy?!

09:31.240 --> 09:33.960
I want to scratch the hell out of my back.

09:33.960 --> 09:36.970
No! I'll conquer the itchiness
with sheer willpower!

09:36.970 --> 09:38.650
I am not itchy!

09:39.120 --> 09:41.240
Itchiness is all in the mind!

09:46.530 --> 09:49.500
Excellent. The itchiness is gone.

09:50.130 --> 09:51.070
Kssssshk

09:51.240 --> 09:53.330
I-Impossible!!

09:51.620 --> 09:53.330
I-Impossible!

09:53.330 --> 09:59.330
Stimulus

09:53.330 --> 09:59.330
Nerve

09:54.530 --> 09:58.270
Wh-Why?! The more I think about it,
the itchier it becomes!

09:56.340 --> 09:57.840
Ichy

09:57.840 --> 09:59.320
Itchy

09:59.490 --> 10:02.670
This is no longer mere itchiness.

10:02.670 --> 10:05.590
The itchiness of all of Japan,
no, all of the universe,

10:05.590 --> 10:08.210
has been concentrated on my back!

10:11.580 --> 10:12.770
I want to scratch it.

10:12.770 --> 10:14.820
I want to scratch it so badly.

10:16.640 --> 10:17.510
My chance!

10:25.510 --> 10:27.370
I'm saved.

10:27.370 --> 10:29.180
Now, I must prepare!

10:30.190 --> 10:31.480
Oh no!!

10:31.760 --> 10:35.890
O-Oh no! I've been left
completely defenseless!

10:37.450 --> 10:38.800
Roar

10:37.770 --> 10:39.510
It's going to eat me!

10:40.940 --> 10:41.700
Ka-chak

10:41.740 --> 10:43.010
Ka-chak

10:45.490 --> 10:46.770
Whomp

10:51.630 --> 10:54.770
Tremble...
Tremble...

10:52.130 --> 10:55.420
The ultimate weapon and ultimate armor...

10:57.370 --> 10:59.970
Glasses!

11:01.780 --> 11:04.480
One

11:01.900 --> 11:04.480
One, two, three, four.

11:02.410 --> 11:04.480
Two

11:03.280 --> 11:04.480
Three

11:03.910 --> 11:04.480
Four

11:04.930 --> 11:08.020
Two, two, three, four.

11:08.020 --> 11:11.040
Three, two, three, four.

11:11.040 --> 11:14.090
Four, two, three, four.

11:14.090 --> 11:16.230
Huh? No objection this time?

11:17.400 --> 11:19.890
Soma-senpai's still not here?

11:22.290 --> 11:24.090
Everyone! Sorry for the wait.

11:22.290 --> 11:24.100
Boom!

11:24.090 --> 11:26.230
President, you're seriously la—

11:25.550 --> 11:26.540
Boom!

11:26.230 --> 11:29.590
We weren't waiting. We just got here.

11:29.590 --> 11:32.410
Let's try the new flavor of cream puffs.

11:32.410 --> 11:34.180
They're tapioca-agar-flavored.

11:36.640 --> 11:39.370
Mm, they're good!

11:39.370 --> 11:41.380
How are they different from usual?

11:41.380 --> 11:45.760
Soma-senpai, please try this tea.
I put 200% of my love into it!

11:46.130 --> 11:49.810
By the way, president. You're
not afraid of anything, right?

11:49.810 --> 11:52.820
Even if he is, he wouldn't tell
some jerk in fake glasses.

12:00.960 --> 12:02.040
Glasses.

12:02.200 --> 12:04.280
So deep...

12:02.810 --> 12:04.250
So deep!

12:31.770 --> 12:36.770
It's an ultrasonic cleaner for glasses with lenses.

12:37.180 --> 12:39.040
Quit slacking off, Takuma!

12:39.040 --> 12:41.610
What did we borrow this bike for?!

12:41.610 --> 12:42.560
I know!

12:42.560 --> 12:45.970
It's so that we could work
together to charge up

12:45.970 --> 12:49.150
the X-Ray Glasses
Mk. 36 all at once!

12:49.150 --> 12:51.420
That's right, Fake Glasses!

12:51.420 --> 12:52.410
Don't butt in!

12:56.190 --> 12:58.080
Akira, are things
becoming see-through?

12:59.050 --> 13:01.740
Not yet. We still
don't have enough po—

13:03.920 --> 13:07.190
They're starting to
respond! Takuma! Pedal!

13:07.190 --> 13:09.260
If I have to...

13:09.650 --> 13:11.600
Almost there! Let's go!

13:12.100 --> 13:16.480
Glasses cluuuub!

13:19.980 --> 13:21.480
Glasses!

13:21.480 --> 13:23.930
Failure is the bridge to success.

13:23.930 --> 13:25.690
Failure is the bridge to success.

13:25.690 --> 13:28.620
Minabe-senpai, you won't
finish at that pace.

13:29.100 --> 13:30.620
Stare.

13:33.580 --> 13:36.930
Soma-senpai! You weren't
hurt, were you?

13:36.930 --> 13:37.750
No problems.

13:37.750 --> 13:39.110
To the contrary, despite being in

13:39.110 --> 13:41.500
direct proximity to the explosion,
there's not a scratch on them!

13:41.980 --> 13:43.440
My glasses are brilliant!

13:43.800 --> 13:45.420
My glasses are all-powerful!

13:45.730 --> 13:48.620
My glasses take the gold medal!

13:48.620 --> 13:50.510
You're shining too brightly, Senpai!

13:51.310 --> 13:54.590
Yukiya! My glasses are all-powerful!

13:57.740 --> 13:59.490
What are you doing, Takuma?

14:00.150 --> 14:03.010
I wanted to take it for a ride.

14:03.010 --> 14:04.190
Don't take off on your own!

14:04.190 --> 14:05.700
That's right!

14:05.700 --> 14:08.730
We need to return that
to Mr. Shirogane!

14:08.730 --> 14:10.780
I'm supposed to be in the front!

14:10.780 --> 14:11.700
That's the problem?!

14:11.700 --> 14:15.650
Senpai! I'll go with you!

14:20.540 --> 14:23.330
Let me on too!

14:34.840 --> 14:36.680
This feels great!

14:42.040 --> 14:43.820
This is fun!

14:52.420 --> 14:54.350
We really rode far!

14:54.350 --> 14:55.080
Yes.

14:55.080 --> 14:57.580
This was a convenient
place for a glasses store.

14:58.710 --> 15:00.540
My lenses are restored.

15:00.540 --> 15:03.290
Minabe-kun, let me in already.

15:07.660 --> 15:09.410
They're all clean now!

15:14.940 --> 15:17.850
Hey. Are you making fun of us?

15:18.650 --> 15:20.310
Soma-senpai!

15:20.310 --> 15:23.690
Hayato's using the cleaner even
though he doesn't have lenses!

15:23.690 --> 15:25.110
Is that true, Mitsuki?

15:25.110 --> 15:27.250
But these are glasses too!

15:27.250 --> 15:29.490
It's an ultrasonic cleaner
for glasses with lenses.

15:29.490 --> 15:30.450
That's right.

15:31.090 --> 15:34.160
You could not understand
the joy it brings us.

15:34.160 --> 15:36.950
We see the whole world clearly now.

15:36.950 --> 15:40.240
Just because I don't have lenses...

15:40.240 --> 15:41.680
Listen, Hayato.

15:41.680 --> 15:46.410
Those rash actions of yours wound
glasses-wearers everywhere.

15:46.410 --> 15:48.590
The Glasses God is
sure to be enraged.

15:49.070 --> 15:50.640
Glasses!

15:50.640 --> 15:52.590
What's the Glasses God?

15:57.190 --> 15:58.550
It looks like it might rain.

15:58.960 --> 16:00.770
Senpai, that way!

16:00.770 --> 16:04.370
That rift in the clouds
is shaped like glasses!

16:04.370 --> 16:05.770
What? Where?

16:05.770 --> 16:07.140
There!

16:11.280 --> 16:12.850
Amazing!

16:12.850 --> 16:14.470
It's a miracle of nature.

16:14.470 --> 16:16.150
Picture, picture!

16:21.770 --> 16:23.790
Hear me, Kimata Hayato.

16:24.370 --> 16:27.560
You have shown contempt for glasses.

16:27.560 --> 16:29.440
Shown contempt? How?

16:29.440 --> 16:33.260
Silence! You can say nothing
to silence my wrath!

16:33.260 --> 16:35.140
You pretend glasses-wearer!

16:35.140 --> 16:38.140
Until you die... Until you die...

16:38.660 --> 16:41.080
You will be cursed!

16:43.650 --> 16:44.640
Hey.

16:45.360 --> 16:46.960
... is what he said!

16:46.960 --> 16:49.910
... is <i>not</i> what he said!

16:49.910 --> 16:52.670
<i>You're</i> the one who said
it! Knock it off already!

16:52.670 --> 16:54.530
It was not!

16:54.530 --> 16:56.430
It was the Glasses God!

16:56.430 --> 16:57.910
But since you wear fake glasses

16:57.910 --> 17:00.660
I figured you couldn't
hear the Glasses God,

17:00.660 --> 17:02.160
so I decided to interpret.

17:02.160 --> 17:06.170
Fake Fake Fake Fake

17:02.680 --> 17:06.170
Fake fake fake fake fake glasses?!

17:07.920 --> 17:12.090
What's wrong with
wearing fake glasses?!

17:12.840 --> 17:15.390
Fake glasses are awesome!

17:16.050 --> 17:17.740
I'm impressed that he
can stay out there.

17:16.050 --> 17:19.390
Fake glasses <i>are</i> glasses!

17:17.740 --> 17:20.990
He can do things like that
because he wears fake glasses.

17:21.770 --> 17:23.810
Hayato character
assassination complete.

17:24.120 --> 17:27.200
Even a little bit of rain
ruins glasses, after all.

17:27.800 --> 17:29.360
Hey.

17:29.360 --> 17:31.910
There's something I've
been thinking for a while.

17:35.430 --> 17:38.570
When rain hits your glasses
and you open your umbrella,

17:39.370 --> 17:42.610
most other people don't
have theirs open, right?

17:43.020 --> 17:44.930
I wonder why that is?

17:45.410 --> 17:48.580
Glasses wearers become aware
of the rain faster than others.

17:49.240 --> 17:51.090
It's a lonely moment, isn't it?

17:51.090 --> 17:54.890
When I think of rainy days, I think
of getting onto packed train cars.

17:57.540 --> 18:00.610
<i>I... I can't see.</i>

18:01.250 --> 18:03.990
It was so crowded I couldn't
get out my glasses cleaner.

18:03.990 --> 18:07.280
I felt humiliated until
the clouding cleared up.

18:08.480 --> 18:11.610
On rainy days, when I go
walking with my umbrella...

18:17.130 --> 18:20.370
The pole of the umbrella bumps
against my frames repeatedly.

18:20.940 --> 18:24.450
And now we have to
deal with a bike.

18:30.130 --> 18:33.750
<i>Damn it!</i>

18:35.790 --> 18:37.550
What are we supposed to do?!

18:37.550 --> 18:38.850
Senpai...

18:38.850 --> 18:40.060
Soma-kun...

18:40.060 --> 18:40.960
Akira.

18:41.950 --> 18:42.760
What is it?

18:44.410 --> 18:50.020
Wiper
Glasses

18:46.250 --> 18:48.100
They're wiper glasses.

18:48.100 --> 18:50.020
Still in the testing stages, but...

18:50.420 --> 18:52.180
What are you going to do?

18:53.110 --> 18:55.020
I will ride in the lead.

18:55.020 --> 18:57.370
The rest of you can
press your heads against

18:57.370 --> 18:59.110
the handlebars to shield
your own glasses.

18:59.110 --> 19:02.590
You're asking us to put our trust
in you and pedal as hard as we can?

19:05.990 --> 19:07.970
It's a big responsibility.

19:07.970 --> 19:10.790
Nevertheless, are you
prepared to face it?

19:13.070 --> 19:15.040
Let's start a revolution.

19:16.420 --> 19:19.550
Don't leave me all by myself.

19:28.930 --> 19:30.100
Are you okay, Yukiya?!

19:32.580 --> 19:34.660
Akira, your speed...

19:34.660 --> 19:35.780
More speed?!

20:12.050 --> 20:14.700
The rain's really not letting up.

20:14.700 --> 20:17.360
Once it gets dark, it'll be
even harder to get home.

20:17.360 --> 20:18.020
Huh?

20:20.570 --> 20:22.360
The chain slipped.

20:22.840 --> 20:24.560
Takuma-kun!

20:25.660 --> 20:26.530
That voice...

20:30.330 --> 20:32.060
We came looking for you!

20:32.060 --> 20:33.660
You were out so late.

20:33.660 --> 20:35.290
Look at you, soaking wet.

20:35.290 --> 20:36.990
You'll catch cold.

20:39.530 --> 20:40.800
That bark...

20:43.300 --> 20:45.020
Norio-san!

20:45.020 --> 20:46.960
You came to find me!

20:51.790 --> 20:53.290
Hey senpai!

20:53.290 --> 20:54.900
Let's go home together!

20:54.900 --> 20:57.930
Norio-san brought two umbrellas.

20:57.930 --> 20:59.900
Sure. That should get us home.

21:00.260 --> 21:02.220
It's longer than the
usual bike chain,

21:02.220 --> 21:04.680
which makes it really hard to fix.

21:04.680 --> 21:06.410
Let's get back so I can get to work.

21:06.410 --> 21:09.410
Okay! I fixed it!

21:14.440 --> 21:17.680
Did they leave me out again?

21:22.260 --> 21:26.400
Why? It's been like this all day.

21:34.060 --> 21:35.230
It can't be...

21:35.660 --> 21:38.050
The curse?

21:38.050 --> 21:39.470
Glasses!

23:11.930 --> 23:14.260
My glasses are a lot like
the club president's, huh?

23:12.090 --> 23:14.260
Me

23:12.640 --> 23:14.260
Club President

23:14.260 --> 23:17.740
Square celluloid frames and oval
square celluloid frames are nothing alike!

23:15.640 --> 23:22.350
Oval Square
Celluloid Frame

23:17.740 --> 23:19.700
But they both have "square
celluloid frame" in the—

23:19.700 --> 23:21.690
They're completely different.
Totally different!

23:19.850 --> 23:23.630
Completely different!!

23:20.810 --> 23:23.630
Totally different!

23:21.690 --> 23:23.630
Absolutely different!

23:23.630 --> 23:25.960
No Glasses! No Life!

23:30.720 --> 23:33.580
Metal rimless. Tomorrow's horoscope:

23:34.430 --> 23:37.330
Who cares. Just do what you want.
